      "id": 1,
      "text": "Millerstown was first plotted for sale in 1790, making it the first town laid out for sale in the territory that became Perry County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millerstown%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The original land was sold as “Smithfield” to James Gallagher in 1766, though he likely lived there earlier.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millerstown%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "David Miller received a deed on September 1, 1780, and established a settlement and ferry operation there.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millerstown%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Historic Sanborn Fire Insurance Maps of Millerstown from 1886 to 1911 show downtown footprints, businesses, and schools, offering a window into the town’s past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
